WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.020 line:6% position:50% align:center
Eval Harness: a simulated client project, part three of five.

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:15.040 line:6% position:50% align:center
One harness now checks both of the hotel group's assistants the same way: the same cases, metrics and gates, with ninety-five percent intervals on every rate.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:23.150 line:6% position:50% align:center
It reproduces both projects' published numbers from their own recordings, and fresh re-runs at the pinned versions pass every gate.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:29.720 line:6% position:50% align:center
Then I made a realistic bad change on a throwaway branch: two passages instead of five, to save tokens.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:34.640 line:6% position:50% align:center
Retrieval only fell from ninety-eight to ninety-three percent, inside the interval.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.820 line:6% position:50% align:center
The gate still failed, because two questions that always passed now always fail.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.180 line:6% position:50% align:center
The message names them.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.850 line:6% position:50% align:center
The branch was never merged.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:46.670 line:6% position:50% align:center
Here is one: a spa question about a sixteen-year-old.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:50.260 line:6% position:50% align:center
The right passage dropped out, and every metric shows it.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.150 line:6% position:50% align:center
An AI judge rates tone and clarity.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:03.710 line:6% position:50% align:center
I labelled seventy replies by hand, in two blind rounds, the second one full of failures on purpose.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:08.100 line:6% position:50% align:center
Its best kappa was point two nine, well under the bar of point six.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.310 line:6% position:50% align:center
So no judge score is trusted, and none is a gate.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.460 line:6% position:50% align:center
The code, the reports and every decision are linked on screen.
